Findings:

- Line 31: input `outputs/new_topics/x.json` = `{"verdict":"VIABLE","topic":{"stem":"x","name":"X"},"trials":[{"gates":{"g":true},"extracted":{"nct":"NCT00000001","aact_per_arm_counts":{"A":1,"B":1}}}]}`. Consequence: `_arm_order` is not defined or imported in the full file, so the first eligible trial crashes before any snapshot is written.

- Line 26: input trial fragment `{"gates":{},"extracted":{"nct":"NCT00000001","aact_per_arm_counts":{"A":1,"B":1}}}` inside a `VIABLE` topic. Consequence: `all({}.values())` is `True`, so a trial with zero gate evidence is accepted as passing all gates.

- Line 47: input extracted fragment with one absent arm versus real zero, e.g. `{"aact_per_arm_counts":{"A":0}}` and `_arm_order(...) == ["A"]`. Consequence: `(tN or 0) + (cN or 0)` makes absent `cN` indistinguishable from real zero, emitting baseline `0` as if complete.

- Line 70: input `index.html` containing only `<!-- audit-first-section:begin -->` without the generated section/cards. Consequence: the idempotency guard is satisfied by its own marker string and skips the actual insertion work.

- Lines 93-94: input `index.html` = `abc`, with no `</main>`, `</body>`, or `</div>`. Consequence: `rfind("</div>")` returns `-1`, so fallback insertion splices the section before the last byte and corrupts the document.

No proven finding: probe keyed to string a fix removes; instrument reading different copy; selector keyed to corpus form; CRLF/LF text comparison; merged-cell tabulation count; negation dropped; wrapper status code reporting.
